normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            12.68.963   Crow
voting precinct.</span></p>

<p class=CIV-MEM><span style='font-size:12.0pt;font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;text-align:justify;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.010  Petitions to create or dissolve no shooting
areas.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Petitions requesting the council to
create a no shooting area or dissolve an existing no shooting area shall be
filed with the clerk of the council.  Petitions shall contain the signatures of
at least ten elector&#8209;residents of each voting precinct in the area under
consideration. A map and legal description of the area shall be included with
the petitions.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  After petition signatures have been
verified by the elections division, the council shall set a date of hearing. 
Legal notice of the hearing shall be published once in the official county
newspaper and once in a newspaper of general circulation within the proposed
area, at least ten days prior to the hearing.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  If the council finds the formation or
dissolution of the petitioned area to be beneficial to the public health,
safety and general welfare, it shall establish such a no shooting area by
ordinance.  The council shall consider, but is not limited to, the location,
terrain and surrounding land use of the petitioned area.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            D.  It is the intent of the council that the
geographic description of no shooting areas as defined in this chapter remain
in effect even after voter precinct boundaries change.  (Ord. 16286 § 1, 2008: 
Ord. 15971 § 68, 2007:  Ord. 1454 §§ 1 - 3, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.020  Violations - Misdemeanor -
Penalty - Arrest.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  Any person carrying a firearm in a
&quot;No Shooting Area,&quot; under circumstances which manifest intent to
discharge or which indicates that such firearm has been discharged in a
&quot;No Shooting Area,&quot; is guilty of a misdemeanor.  Among those
circumstances which may be considered in determining such intent are the
following:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              1.  Type of firearm;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              2.  Manner in which firearm is being
carried;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              3.  Whether or not the firearm is capable
of discharge;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>              4  Information concerning the discharge of
a firearm within the prior two hours.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The first offense for violation of this
chapter constitutes a civil penalty not to exceed one hundred dollars. 
Consecutive offenses are punishable, upon conviction, by a fine not exceeding
two hundred fifty dollars or by confinement in the county jail for a period of
not more than ninety days.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Any police officer having information to
support a reasonable belief that a person has committed a violation of this
chapter, involving physical harm or threats of harm to any person or property
and by a firearm, has the authority to arrest the person.  (Ord. 1498 §§ 1 - 3,
1973).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.030  Unincorporated King County
where not designated as a &quot;no shooting&quot; area.</b>  In all areas of
King County not designated by ordinance as &quot;no shooting&quot; areas,
except when a person is on the person's own property or has written permission
from the owner, and the discharge of such weapons and the trajectory of any
projectile is restricted to said property, it is unlawful to discharge a
firearm within five hundred feet of any building capable of being occupied by
people or domestic animals or used for storage of flammable or combustible
materials or trails used for hiking, biking, or horseback riding, and
designated as such in the county comprehensive plan; provided, that the above&#8209;referenced
distance shall not be less than two hundred fifty feet when the firearm being
discharged is a shotgun.  (Ord. 18670 § 54, 2018:  Ord. 4691 § 1, 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.040  Citizens may petition to use
firearms in &quot;no shooting&quot; areas at certain times.</b>  In areas
designated &quot;no shooting&quot; by ordinances, citizens may petition
(according to the provisions of Section 12.68.010) to allow the use of firearms
during lawful open hunting seasons, during stated periods of time as
established by the Washington State Game Commission.  (Ord. 4691 § 2, 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.050  Statutory references for
general information.</b>  The provisions of RCW 9A.48.070, RCW 9A.48.080, RCW
9A.48.090, RCW 9.41.230, RCW 9.41.240, RCW 9.41.260, RCW 9.41.270, RCW
77.16.260, WAC 232-12-047 to 051, and WAC 232-12-244 to 247 as amended, all of
which regulate the discharge of weapons, are referenced for general information
purposes.  (Ord. 4691 § 3, 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.070  Violation of Sections 12.68.030
through 12.68.050.</b>  Any violation of Sections 12.68.030 through 12.68.050
is a misdemeanor, and the punishment shall be provided by the laws of the state
of Washington.  (Ord. 4691 § 4, 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.080  Near Lake Sawyer.</b>  The
discharge of all firearms within one thousand yards of the shoreline of Lake
Sawyer in King County is prohibited, with the following exceptions:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The protection of persons and property;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The discharge of firearms on the waters
and within fifteen hundred feet of the shoreline of Lake Sawyer for hunting
purposes shall be illegal for the twelve months of the year:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  For the herding and scaring of waterfowl,
out of season, by the discharge of shotguns by persons holding proper permits
from the United States Fish and Wildlife Service to do so.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            No firearms shall be discharged toward any
residential dwelling within two hundred yards thereof.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Any person who violates the provisions of
this section is guilty of a misdemeanor.  (Res. 36257 (part), 1968: Res. 18931
(part) ).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.090  Near Lake Kilarney.</b>  A
&quot;no shooting&quot; area is established, comprising the following described
area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Sections 21, 22, 27 and 28, Twp. 21 N., R. 4
E., W.M., a radius of approximately one mile from Lake Kilarney.  (Res. 9774
(part), 1945).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.100  Five-mile game preserve area.</b> 
A &quot;no shooting&quot; area is established, comprising the following
described property:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All of that area formerly set aside by the
Washington State Department of Game as the &quot;Five Mile Game Preserve&quot;
and including a portion of the Lake Kilarney &quot;no shooting&quot; area as
established by Section 12.68.020, being further described as follows:
commencing at the intersection of the Milton Road and the King-Pierce County
line in the southwest quarter of Section 32, Twp. 21 N., R. 4 E., W.M., thence
northerly along the Milton Road to an intersection with the Beede Road, thence
east along the centerline of Sections 21 and 22, Twp. 21 N., R. 4 E., W.M.,
which is the Beede Road, to an intersection with the Old Military Road, thence
southerly along the Old Military Road to an intersection with 12th Street in
Sec. 27, Twp. 21 N., R. 4 E., W.M., thence east along 12th Street to an
intersection with Grandview Avenue, Sec. 26, Twp. 21 N., R. 4 E., W.M., thence
south along Grandview Avenue to an intersection with 10th Street, thence west
along 10th Street to an intersection with Kansas Avenue, thence south along
Kansas Avenue to the King-Pierce County line, thence west along the King-Pierce
County line to the point of beginning.  (Res. 9791 (part), 1945).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.110  Near Lake Burien.</b>  Lake
Burien and the land immediately adjoining thereto is closed to the firing of
all firearms at all times.  (Res. 9332, 1944).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.120  Near Lake Haller.</b>  Haller
Lake and the land immediately adjoining thereto is hereby declared closed to
the firing of all firearms at all times.  (Res. 9386, 1944).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.130  In township twenty-one.</b>  A
&quot;no shooting&quot; area is hereby established comprising the following
described property:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All of the W1/2 of Sec. 15, the E1/2 of Sec.
16, the NE1/4 of the NE1/4 of Sec. 21, the NW1/4 of the NW1/4 of Sec. 22, Twp.
21 N., R. 4 E. W.M. (Res. 9408, 1944).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            12.68.140  Area bounded by Renton and Puget
Sound.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  A &quot;no shooting&quot; area is hereby established, commencing at
the intersection of the north line of Section 3, Twp. 23 N., R. 3 E., W.M., and
the shore line of Puget Sound; thence running easterly along the north line of
Section 3, 2 and 1, Twp. 23 N., R. 3 E., W.M., and Sections 6, 5 and 4, Twp. 23
N., R. 4 E., W.M., to the northeast corner of Section 4, Twp. 23 N., R. 4 E.,
W.M., thence south one&#8209;half mile; thence east along the centerline of
Section 3, Twp. 23 N., R. 4 E., W.M., approximately two&#8209;thirds mile to an
intersection with State Road #2 (Dunlap Canyon); thence southeasterly along the
centerline of State Road #2 to an intersection with the west margin of Shattuck
Street (Renton city limits); thence south approximately twenty&#8209;eight
hundred feet along the west margin of Shattuck Street and Shattuck Street
produced to an intersection with the westerly production of the south margin of
8th Avenue (Renton city limits); thence easterly along the south margin of 8th
Avenue produced and 8th Avenue to an intersection with the centerline of State
Road 5&#8209;C (Benson Road); thence south along State Road 5&#8209;C to an
intersection with the east and west centerline of Section 8, Twp. 22 N., R. 5
E., W.M.; thence west along the centerlines of Sections 8 and 7, Twp. 22 N., R.
5 E., W.M., and Sections 12, 11, 10, 9, 8, 7, Twp. 22 N., R. 4 E., W.M., to an
intersection with the shore line of Puget Sound in said Section 7, Twp. 22 N.,
R. 4 E., W.M.; thence northerly along the shore of Puget Sound to the point of
beginning; provided, however, that the discharging of shotguns for hunting
purposes shall be permitted in any area not less than two hundred yards from
any house, building or county right of way.  (Res. 9409, 1949).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.150  Near Bitter Lake.</b>  A
&quot;no shooting&quot; area is hereby established comprising the following
described property:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            An area bounded by Greenwood Avenue on the
west, Aurora Avenue on the east, North 132nd Street on the south and 138th
Street on the north, which includes the small body of non&#8209;navigable water
known as Bitter Lake.  (Res. 9436, 1944).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.160  Sections 7, 8, 16, 17, 18, 20
and 21, Township 21.</b>  A &quot;no shooting&quot; area is hereby established,
comprising the following described property: Secs. 7, 8, 16, 17, 18, 20 and 21,
Twp. 21 N., R. 5 E., W.M. (Res. 9598, 1945).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.170  Near Angle Lake.</b>  A
&quot;no shooting&quot; area is hereby established, comprising the following
described property:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Between South 188th Street on the most
northerly boundary, South 200th Street on the most southerly boundary, Pacific
Highway on the west, and the Military Road to the east, including the waters of
Angle Lake.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Except, however, nothing in this section
shall prohibit the shooting of rodents by owners on their property to prevent
damage to property.  (Res. 9626, 1945).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.180  Area lying northeast of
intersection of east 145th street and</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>15th avenue northeast</span></b><span style='font-family:
"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>.  A &quot;no shooting&quot; area is
hereby established, comprising the following described property:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Commencing at the southwest corner of Section
16, Township 26 North, Range 4 East, W.M., which is the intersection of East
145th Street and 15th Avenue Northeast; thence north on 15th Avenue Northeast
to East 175th Street; thence east on East 175th Street to Ballinger Way (State
Road No. 28); thence southeasterly along Ballinger Way to Bothell Way (State
Road No. 2); thence southwesterly along Bothell Way to East 145th Street;
thence west along East 145th Street to the point of beginning.  (Res. 9832, 1945).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.190  Near Steel Lake.</b>  A
&quot;no shooting&quot; area is hereby established, comprising the following
described property:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All territory within a radius of one mile of
Steel Lake, situated in Sec. 9, Twp. 21 N., R. 4 E., W.M. (Res. 10814, 1948).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.200  Near Cottage Lake.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is hereby prohibited and a &quot;no shooting&quot; area is
established comprising the following described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            On Cottage lake and for a distance back
therefrom of one hundred yards in any direction from the shoreline.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Any person who violates the provisions of
this section is guilty of a misdemeanor.  (Res. 12228, 1950).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.210  Near Hill Top Community.</b> 
The shooting of firearms is hereby prohibited and a &quot;no shooting&quot;
area is established, comprising the following described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Hill Top Community in Secs. 22 and 23, Twp. 24 N., R. 5
E., W.M., King County, Washington.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A plat is recorded in Volume 47, Pages 28 and
29, in the Records Section of King County.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The community is slightly southwest of Lake
Sammamish and is approximately half way between Issaquah and Seattle, situated
on a hilltop about two miles south of the Bellevue Airport.  The access road to
the community is one and three&#8209;tenths miles long, and begins at the
county highway (Old Sunset Highway or Issaquah Road).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Further description is as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the quarter&#8209;section corner
common to Sections 22 and 23; thence N. 88o 16' 54&quot; W. for 1329.52 feet to
the S.W. corner of the SE1/4 of the NE1/4 of said Sec. 22; thence N. 1o 16'
23&quot; E. for 626.34 feet along the west boundary of the SE1/4 of the NE1/4
of said Section 22; thence east for 465.00 feet; thence N. 1o 16' 23&quot; E.
for 840.21 feet; thence N. 67o 23' 00&quot; E. for 390.00 feet; thence east for
270.00 feet; thence S. 69o 00' 00&quot; E. for 240.00 feet; thence S. 49o 26'
00&quot; E. for 16.19 feet to a point on the section line between Secs. 22 and
23 which is N. 1o 17' 13&quot; E. 1559.89 feet from the quarter section corner
common to Sections 22 and 23; thence continuing S. 49o 26' 00&quot; E. for
558.81 feet; thence S. 79o 37' 00&quot; for 272.00 feet; thence south for 1347.01
feet; thence west for 731.58 feet to a point on the section line between said
Sections 22 and 23; thence N. 1o 17' 13&quot; E. along said section line for
200.00 feet to the point of beginning.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Any person who violates the provisions of this section is
guilty of a misdemeanor.  (Res. 12271, 1950).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.220  Lake Sammamish Area.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no&#8209;shooting area is established
in and around the Lake Sammamish area lying within unincorporated King County
and comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All the waters of Lake Sammamish and the area
surrounding the lake for a distance of five hundred feet; except the no&#8209;shooting
area specifically described in Resolution 19638, K.C.C. 12.68.340, and except
those areas within city limits and controlled by city no&#8209;shooting
ordinances, and except those areas within the boundaries of Marymoor Park and
Lake Sammamish State Park.  (Ord. 6819, 1984).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            12.68.230  Area southwest of Renton and near
Lake Boren.</span></b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>  A &quot;no shooting area&quot; is hereby established comprising the
following described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that portion of Sections 27, 28, 33 and
34, Twp. 24 N., R. 5 E., W.M., contained within the following described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Commencing at the intersection of George
Sparling Road #869 and Chas. S. Custer Road #89 in the southeast quarter of
Section 28; thence southerly along the centerline of said Custer Road to its
end; thence southeasterly, easterly and northeasterly two hundred sixty feet
south of and parallel to the south edge of Lake Boren to the centerline of the
Renton&#8209;Newcastle Road #1019; thence northerly along said Renton&#8209;Newcastle
Road to the said George Sparling road; thence westerly along said Sparling Road
to the point of beginning.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Any person who violates the provisions of
this section is guilty of a misdemeanor.  (Res. 12914, 1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.240  Near Lake Dolloff.</b>  A
&quot;no shooting area&quot; is hereby established comprising the following
described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that portion of Secs. 3, 4, 9 and 10,
Twp. 21 N., R. 4 E., W.M., lying within a line 600 feet distant from the shore
line of Lake Dolloff.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Any person who violates the provisions of
this section is guilty of a misdemeanor.  (Res. 12939, 1951).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

