designated a &quot;no shooting&quot; area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            That portion of Sections 29 and 32 of Twp. 22
N., R. 4E., W.M.; and Sections 5 and 6 of Twp. 21 N., R. 4E., W.M.; and Section
1 of Twp. 21 N., R. 3E., W.M. described as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the intersection of the north
line of Government Lot No. 2 of said Section 29 with the north&#8209;south
centerline of said Section 29;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Thence southerly along the north&#8209;south
centerlines of said Sections 29, 32, and 5 to the center of said Section 5;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Thence westerly along the east&#8209;west
centerline of said Sections 5, 6, and 1 to an intersection with the low tide
line of Puget Sound;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Thence easterly and northerly along said low
tide line to an intersection with the north line of Government Lot No. 2 of
said Section 29;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Thence easterly along said north line of
Government Lot No. 2 to the point of beginning.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Any person violating this section is guilty
of a misdemeanor.  (Ord. 262 §§ 1, 2, 1969).</span></p>

