North, Range 6 East, W.M., lying westerly of 196th Avenue S.E., easterly of
188th Avenue S.E., northerly of S.E. 304th Street and southerly of S.E. 290th
Street.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Any person who violates the provisions of
this section is guilty of a misdemeanor.  (Ord. 1146 §§ 1 and 2, 1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.570  Lake Retreat.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The shooting of firearms is prohibited in
the following area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The waters of Lake Retreat and that portion
of land lying between the shoreline of Lake Retreat and a line two hundred
yards (as measured in an upland direction) from and parallel to S.E. 276th
Street, S.E. 280th Street (S.E. Lake Retreat Road) and Lake Retreat-Kanaskat
Road.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The prohibition described in A.  herein
shall not apply in cases involving the protection of persons and property.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            C.  Any person who violates the provisions of
this section is guilty of a misdemeanor.  (Ord. 1408 § 1, 1972; Ord. 1347 § 1,
1972).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.580  Lake Joy.</b>  The shooting of
firearms is prohibited in the following area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The waters of Lake Joy and the portion of
land lying between the shoreline of Lake Joy and a line five hundred yards from
and parallel to that portion of the Lake Joy road surrounding the lake.  (Ord.
1554 § 1, 1973).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.590  Sections 27, 33 and 34,
township 22.</b>  The shooting of firearms is prohibited in the following area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            That portion of Sections 27, 33 and 34,
Township 22 North, Range 6 East, W.M., lying south of Kent-Kangley Road (SR
516); north of S.E. 288th Street; west of Renton&#8209;Enumclaw Highway (SR
169); and east of the west section line of Section 33 which is approximately
one&#8209;fourth mile west of 216th Avenue S.E., less portion described in
Resolution No. 36257 and Resolution No. 18931 (Section 12.68.010).  (Ord. 1670
§ 1, 1973).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.600  Coalfield area.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited in the Coalfield area, described as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that area lying easterly of 136th Avenue
S.E.; southwesterly of 144th Place S.E. and County Road No. 72; and northerly
of S.E. Coalfield Road.  (Ord. 1779 § 1, 1973).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            12.68.610  Twin Lakes precinct.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The shooting of
firearms is prohibited in the Twin Lakes Precinct, described as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the intersection of the
centerline of 47th Ave. S.W. also known as F.B. Hoyt Road S.W. and the
centerline of S.W. 320th St.; thence easterly along the centerline of S.W.
320th St. to the centerline intersection of 36th Ave. S.W.; thence southerly to
the northeast corner of Lot 171 of Twin Lakes No. 2 as recorded in Vol. 79 of
Plats, pages 32 to 37, Records of King County, Washington; thence south along
the east line of said Lot 171 and its southerly extension to the centerline of
S.W. 325th St.; thence westerly along said centerline and continuing
southwesterly along the centerline of 39th Place S.W. and the centerline of
40th Ave. S.W. to the centerline of S.W. 328th St.; thence west along the
centerline of S.W. 328th St. a distance of 128 feet to a point on the west line
of the plat of Twin Lakes No. 3 (Vol. 82, pages 42 to 44); thence south along
said west line to the centerline of Section 14, Twp. 21 N., Range 3 E., W.M.;
thence west along said centerline to the centerline of 47th Ave. S.W.; thence
northerly along the centerline of 47th Ave. S.W. to the centerline of S.W.
320th St. and the point of beginning.  (Ord. 1844 § 1, 1973).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.620  Beaver Lake.</b>  The shooting
of firearms is prohibited and a &quot;No Shooting&quot; area is established
comprising the following described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All of the waters of the chain of three
Beaver Lakes and adjacent lands for a distance of 500 feet from the shores of
any point on the lakes, all in Section 1, 2 and 11, Township 24 North, R 6,
EWM, King County, Washington.  (Res. 16688 (part), 1956).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.630  Cherry Garden Division No. 2.</b> 
The shooting of firearms is prohibited, except by licensed hunters during
regular hunting season, in parts of Cherry Garden Division No. 2 described as;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Lots 65 through 66 and Lots 80 through 86,
Section 9, Township 26 North, Range 7 East, W.M.  (Ord. 18670 § 55, 2018:  Ord.
1937 § 1, 1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.640  Lake Youngs Reservation.  </b>The
shooting of firearms is prohibited in the Lake Youngs Reservation described as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The south half of Section 35; the west half
of the southwest quarter and the west half of the southeast quarter, of the
southwest quarter, of Section 36, all in Twp. 23 N., R. 5 E., W.M.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Section 1 except Government Lots 1 and 2 and
except the east half of the southeast quarter of the northeast quarter and
except any of the remainder of said section lying northeasterly of Petrovitsky
Road S.E.; Section 2; Section 11 except the southwest quarter and except the
southwest quarter of the southeast quarter; Section 12 except the southeast
quarter and except the south half of the northeast quarter and except the
southeast quarter of the southwest quarter; all in Twp. 22N., R. 5 E., W.M.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Portion of Government Lot 6 lying
southwesterly of Petrovitsky Road S.E. and all of Government Lot 7, Section 6;
Government Lot 1, Section 7; all in Twp. 22 N., R. 6 E., W.M. (Ord. 2022 § 1,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.650  Shadow Lake.</b>  The shooting
of firearms on and around Shadow Lake is prohibited.  The area to be closed is
described as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All of the southeast quarter of Section 7,
Twp. 22 N., R. 6 E., W.M. lying west of 196th Avenue S.E. (Ord. 2039 § 1,
1974).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.660  Adair precinct.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited in and around a portion of the Adair
precinct described as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that portion of Section 22, Twp. 26 N.,
R. 5 E., W.M., lying westerly of the Burlington Northern Railway right&#8209;of&#8209;way. 
(Ord. 2353 § 1, 1975).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.670  Cottage Lake, Millikin and Mink
Road precincts.</b>  The shooting of firearms is prohibited in and around a
