Sound Power and Light Company substation located northwesterly of the
intersection of Veazie&#8209;Cumberland Road and S.E. 352nd Street; bound on
the north one&#8209;fourth mile north of S.E. 352nd Street.  (Ord. 2700 § 1,
1976).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            12.68.690  Stillwater precinct.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The shooting of
firearms is prohibited in and around a portion of Stillwater precinct described
as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The west three&#8209;quarters of Section 33
lying east of Fay Road N.E. and the south one&#8209;half of Section 28 lying
south of Fay Road N.E. and N.E. Big Rock Road, except the southeast one&#8209;quarter
of the southeast one&#8209;quarter of said Section 28, Township 26 N., Range 7
E., W.M. (Ord. 3196 § 1, 1977).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            12.68.700  Four Lakes precinct.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The shooting of
firearms is prohibited in and around a portion of Four lakes precinct described
as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            That portion of Section 27, 28, and 33,
Township 23 north, Range 6 east, W.M. with a description as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that area within 1,500 feet of Cedar
Grove Road Southeast, also known as J. W. Carr Co. Road No. 877, lying
northeasterly of the Cedar Grove Road Southeast and Southeast Lake Francis Road
intersection and Southwesterly of the Bonneville transmission line.  (Ord. 3587
§ 1, 1978).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.710  Clay precinct.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited in and around a portion of Clay precinct
described as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            That portion of Government Lots 1 and 2
Section 2, Township 21 North, Range 5 East, in King County, Washington, lying
northwesterly of the Northern Pacific Railroad right&#8209;of&#8209;way and
northeasterly of the Soo's Creek Berrydale Road, except the north 165 feet of
the west 264 feet of said lot 2. (Ord. 3630 § 1, 1978).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.720  Gold Creek area.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited in and around the Gold Creek area, the Gold
Creek Athletic Center, described as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            That portion of Section 15, Township 26
North, Range 5 East, W.M., lying East of the East Channel of the Sammamish
Waterway also known as Drainage Ditch No. 3 and West of the West right of way
margin of Morris Road also known as 140th Place Northeast and South of the
North line of the sixty&#8209;foot strip of land which is north of, continuous
and parallel to the north line of the South 65/160th of the northeast quarter
of said Sections.  (Ord. 4133 § 1, 1979).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.730  Woodinville&#8209;Redmond area.</b> 
The shooting of firearms is prohibited in and around the Woodinville&#8209;Redmond
area, described as:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All the area of King County bounded on the
north by the centerline of Woodinville&#8209;Duvall Road; bounded on the east
by the centerline of West Snoqualmie Valley Road; bounded on the south by
Novelty Hill Road and bounded on the west by Avondale Road; except those
portions incorporated into the City of Redmond and except that portion previously
established as a &quot;No Shooting Area&quot; by Section 12.68.620.  (Ord. 4335
§ 1, 1979).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.740  Portion of Stacy precinct.</b> 
The shooting of firearms, in accordance with general law, is allowed in and
around a portion of Stacy precinct defined as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that portion of unincorporated King
County, Washington, lying within Sections 23 and 26 and the Southeast quarter
of Section 27, Township 22 North, Range 4 East, W.M.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Also that portion of the north half of
Section 35, said Township and Range lying easterly and northerly of the
centerline of South 272nd Way and South 277th Street.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Except any portion thereof lying within 500
feet of the bank of the Green River.  (Ord. 4508 § 1, 1979).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.750  Jovita Heights&#8209;Spider
Lake.  </b>The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a &quot;no shooting&quot;
area is established comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that portion of Section 26 and Section
27, Township 21 N., Range 4 E., W.M. lying westerly of the corporate city
limits of Algona and Pacific; except that portion previously designated
&quot;no shooting&quot; by King County Resolution No. 9791;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Provided, that property owners or their
designated representative may discharge weapons using blank round ammunition as
part of the process of training hunting dogs.  (Ord. 4761 § 1, 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.760  Norway Hill.  </b>The shooting
of firearms is prohibited and a no shooting area is established comprising the
following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the City limit of Bothell where
it meets the centerline of NE 145th Street at 100th Avenue NE; thence easterly
along the centerline of NE 145th Street to the centerline intersection of 105th
Avenue NE; thence northerly along the centerline of 105th Avenue NE to the
intersection of the quarter section line between the Northwest and Southwest
quarters of Section 17, Township 26 North, Range 5 East, W.M.; thence easterly
along said quarter section line to the quarter section corner at the center of
said Section 17; thence northerly along the quarter section line between the
Northwest and Northeast quarters of said section to its intersection with the
northerly boundary of the Tolt River Pipeline right&#8209;of&#8209;way; thence
approximately northeasterly in a straight line to the centerline intersection
of 108th Avenue NE and NE 164th Place (at the hairpin turn); thence easterly
along the centerline of NE 164th Place to the centerline intersection of 112th
Avenue NE; thence northerly along the centerline of 112th Avenue NE and its
extension 112th Place NE to the City limit of Bothell; thence generally
westerly and southerly along the City limit of Bothell to the point of
beginning.  (Ord. 5592 § 1, 1981).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.770  Maple Valley.</b>  The shooting
of firearms is prohibited and a no shooting area is established comprising the
following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The South 1/2 of the East 3/4 of Section 4,
Township 22 N., Range 6 E., W.M., lying Westerly of the center of the Cedar
River; TOGETHER with and including the following Lots of Maple Valley Farms
(Volume 27 of Plats, page 39):  Lots 15, 16, 17 and 18 ALSO Lots 19 through 28
of said Maple Valley Farms and their extension to the center of the Cedar
River.  </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The department of </span><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>natural resources and parks<span
style='letter-spacing:-.1pt'> is hereby instructed to install No Shooting Area
signs on the perimeter of this area immediately.  (Ord. 14199 § 171, 2001: 
Ord. 5991 § 2, 1982).</span></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.780  Cumberland &#8209; Fish Lake &#8209;
Green River.</b>  The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no shooting area
is established comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All that portion of Section 30, Township 21
North, Range 7 East, W.M., lying easterly of the east right&#8209;of&#8209;way
margin of the Enumclaw&#8209;Franklin Road.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>Together with the north 1/2 of Section 31, Township 21
North, Range 7 East, W.M.; EXCEPT that portion lying northwesterly of the
southeasterly right&#8209;of&#8209;way margin of said Enumclaw&#8209;Franklin
Road (aka County Road #1017), all situated in King County, Washington.  (Ord.
6693, 1984).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.790  Issaquah&#8209;Fall City Road
Area.</b>  The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no&#8209;shooting area
is established within Sunny Hills and Gilman precincts in and around the
vicinity of the western half of the Issaquah&#8209;Fall City Road lying within
unincorporated King County and comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All of the following area of TWp. 24 N.,
Range 6 E., W.M.:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            The south half of Section 12; all of Sections
13, 14 and 15; all of Section 22 except that part previously established as a
&quot;no&#8209;shooting area&quot; by Section 12.68.330; all of Section 23; all
of Sections 26 and 27 that lie north of interstate highway No. 90, except that
portion of incorporated into the City of Issaquah.  (Ord. 6736, 1984).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.800  Boulevard Lane Park Area.</b> 
The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no&#8209;shooting area is
established within Fuller, Wanda and Griffith precincts, and a portion of Iowa
precinct in and around the Boulevard Lane Park area lying within unincorporated
King County and comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All the area within those portions of
Sections 27, 28, 33 and 34, Township 23 N., Range 5 E., W.M., King County,
Washington, lying easterly of 116th Avenue S.E., southerly of S.E. Petrovitsky
Road, westerly of 140th Avenue S.E. and northerly of S.E. 192nd Street.  (Ord.
6810, 1984).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.810  Tiger Mountain Area.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no&#8209;shooting area is established
with Gilman, Tiger Mountain, Mirrormont, Haas, Hutchinson, and Preston
precincts in and around the vicinity of the Tiger Mountain Area, lying within
unincorporated King County and comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Those portions of Townships 23 and 24, Range
6 East, W.M. TOGETHER with those portions of Townships 23 and 24, Range 7 East,
W.M., King County, Washington described as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the intersection of the South
region of SR 90 and West margin of SR 18, said point being located in Township
23, Range 7 East; thence generally Southwesterly along said West margin of SR
18 to its intersection with the Northeasterly margin of the Issaquah&#8209;Hobart
Road, said point being located in Sec. 36, Township 23, Range 6 East; thence
generally Northerly along said margin of Issaquah Hobart Road to its
intersection with the City Limits of Issaquah as established by city ordinance
855; thence Easterly, Northerly, Easterly, Northerly and Northwesterly along
said city limits to the East line of that area annexed to the City of Issaquah
by city ordinance 725; thence North and West along said city limits to the West
margin of Northern Pacific Railroad (abandoned); thence Northerly along said
margin to its intersection with the South margin of SR 90; thence Easterly
along said South margin to the West margin of SR 18 and point of beginning. 
Except as follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  All portions already provided for by King
County Resolution 28537 and exceptions thereto;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  All portions thereof lying within Tiger
Mountain State Forest.  (Ord. 6998, 1984).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.820  Ravensdale Area.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited and no&#8209;shooting area is established
within Ravensdale voting precinct comprising the following legally described
area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            All of sections 30 and 31, Township 22 North,
Range 7 East, W.M., together with all of section 36, Township 22 North, Range 6
East, W.M., together with the West 1/2 section of section 29, Township 22
North, Range 7 East, W.M., together with that portion of section 32, Township
22 North, Range 7 East, W.M., lying westerly of the southeast margin of the
Kent&#8209;Kangley Road and the easterly margin of the Retreat&#8209;Kanaskat
Rd.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Except for any portion thereof described in
King County Ordinance No. 1408 and presently recognized as a &quot;No&#8209;Shooting
Area&quot;.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            And except any portion owned or leased by the
Cascade Rifle and Pistol Club and the Georgetown Rod and Gun Club which may be
located within the above described area.  (Ord. 7074, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            12.68.825  Ravensdale voting precinct.</span></b><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>  The shooting of
firearms is prohibited and a no shooting area is established within the
Ravensdale voting precinct, comprising the following area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>All of the area bounded by the intersection of the north
margin of the Kent-Kangley Road (SR 516) and the western margin of the
Retreat-Kanaskat Road; thence, southeasterly along the Retreat-Kanaskat Road to
the intersection of the southern margin of the Retreat-Kanaskat Road and the
southern margin of the Kanaskat-Kangley Road; thence northeasterly to the
intersection of the northern margin of the Kanaskat-Kangley Road and the
eastern margin of the Kent-Kangley Road (SR 516); thence, westerly along the
Kent-Kangley Road (SR 516) to the Point of Beginning.  (Ord. 14891 § 1, 2004).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.826  Ravensdale voting precinct -
Section 35, Township 22 North, Range 6 East, W.M.</b></span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            A.  The shooting of firearms is prohibited
and a no shooting area is established within the Ravensdale voting precinct.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            B.  The area is all of Section 35, Township
22 North, Range 6 East, W.M.  The area is bounded by SE 272 ST on the north,
244 Avenue on the west, SE 288 Street on the south and 260 Avenue SE on the
east.  (Ord. 15510 § 1, 2006).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.830  High Valley Area.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no-shooting area is established within
High Valley voting precinct comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            That portion of Sections 6, 7, 8, 9, 16 and
17, Township 23 North, Range 6 East, W.M. King County, Washington described as
follows:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the intersection of the North
margin of SE May Valley Road and the Southeast margin of SR 900 (Renton
Issaquah Road SE); thence Northeasterly along said margin of SR 900 to the East
line of said Section 6; thence South along the East line of Section 6 to the
Southeast corner thereof; thence East along the North line of Section 8 and 9
to the Northeast corner of Section 9; thence South along the East line of said
Section 9 and Section 16 to its intersection with the north margin of said SE May
Valley Road; thence generally Northwesterly along said North margin to the
Point of Beginning.  (Ord. 7075, 1985).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.840  Mathew and Tiger Mountain.</b> 
The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no&#8209;shooting area is
established within portions of Mathew and Tiger Mountain precincts lying within
unincorporated King County and comprising the following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the intersection of the south
margin of S.E. May Valley Road and the west margin of Issaquah&#8209;Hobart
Road S.E., then southerly along Issaquah&#8209;Hobart Road S.E. to the
intersection of Issaquah&#8209;Hobart Road S.E. and the north margin of Cedar
Grove Road S.E., then southwesterly along Cedar Grove Road S.E. to the
intersection of Cedar Grove Road S.E. and the east margin of 228th Avenue S.E.,
then northerly along 228th Avenue S.E. to the entrance to the King County solid
waste division's Cedar Hills Landfill, then northerly along the fenced boundary
of the Cedar Hills Landfill to the northeast corner of the landfill boundary
fence, then west along the Cedar Hills Landfill boundary fence to the intersection
of the Cedar Hills Landfill boundary fence and the east right of way margin of
Puget Sound Power and Light Company's Sammamish&#8209;Maple Valley transmission
line (formerly called Bonneville Power Administration Covington&#8209;Chief
Joseph Number One Transmission Line), then northerly along the Sammamish&#8209;Maple
Valley Transmission Line to the point where the Sammamish&#8209;Maple Valley
Transmission Line crosses the south margin of S.E. May Valley Road, then
northeasterly along S.E. May Valley Road to the intersection of S.E. May Valley
Road and Issaquah&#8209;Hobart Road S.E., the point of beginning.  All being
located in Sections 15, 16, 21, 22, 27 and 28, TWP 23 North, RGE 6 East, W.M.,
King County, Washington.  (Ord. 7940, 1987).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.850  Bear Creek, Union Hill and
Vincent precincts.</b>  The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no&#8209;shooting
area is established within portions of the Bear Creek, Union Hill and Vincent
voting precincts lying within unincorporated King County and comprising the
following legally described area:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the intersection of the East
margin of 208th Avenue NE with the North margin of NE Union Hill Road, said
point being located in Section 8, Township 25 North, Range 6 East, W.M. King
County Washington, then North along said East margin of 208th Avenue NE to the
South margin of NE Novelty Hill Road, then Northeasterly along the southerly
margin of NE Novelty Hill Road to the Southwesterly margin of West Snoqualmie
Valley Road NE, then Southeasterly along the Southwesterly margin of West Snoqualmie
Valley Road NE to its intersection with the West margin of Ames Lake Carnation
Road NE, then Southerly along said West margin of Ames Lake Carnation Road NE
to the North margin of the NE Union Hill Road, then Northwesterly along the
North margin of the NE Union Hill Road to the East margin of 208th Avenue NE
and point of beginning.  Less any portion already designated as a no&#8209;shooting
area as identified in Resolution 26754 and known as the Ames Lake District. 
(Ord. 8550, 1988).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.860  Cumberland vicinity.</b>  The
shooting of firearms is prohibited and a &quot;no shooting&quot; area is
established comprising the following described property: Beginning at the NW
corner of Section 22, Township 21 North, Range 7 East; thence east to the NE
corner of Section 22, Township 21 North, Range 7 East; thence south to the
Weyerhaeuser White River Main Line Haul Road; thence, southwesterly to the
south boundary of Section 34, Township 21 North, Range 7 East; thence, west to
the intersection of SE 384th and the Kanaskat-Cumberland Road to the true point
of beginning.  (Ord. 10318, 1992).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.870  Old Red Brick Road and Johnson
Park vicinity.</b>  The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no-shooting
area is established in an area, known as the Old Red Brick Road - Johnson Park
area, within the Bear Creek and Mabel voting precincts, contained by the
following boundaries:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Novelty Hill Road on the north; 204th Place
Northeast and 208th Avenue Northeast on the east; Redmond-Fall City Road on the
South; and the Redmond city limits on the west.  (Ord. 11384 § 1, 1994).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.68.880  Greenwater River vicinity.</b> 
The shooting of firearms is prohibited and a no-shooting area of approximately
220 acres is established within township 19 north, range 9 east, in portions of
sections 2, 3, 4, 10, and 11, within the Chinook voting precinct, comprising
the following described property:</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            Beginning at the intersection of State Route
410 and Weyerhaeuser Road 6400 (Forest Service Road 7125) northerly and
easterly along Weyerhaeuser Road 6400 to the intersection of Weyerhaeuser Road
6401 (Forest Service Road 7130). Then easterly along Weyerhaeuser Road 6401 
to  the  west line  of Section 2. Then to Weyerhaeuser Road 8012-3B and
continuing easterly to the center of the stream bed intersecting Road 8012-3B
at the North-South 1/16 section line of the NW 1/4 of Section 11.  Then south
along said stream bed to the King-Pierce County Boundary, which is the center
of the Greenwater River, then westerly along the center of the Greenwater River
and the White River to a point in line with the intersection of SR 410 and Road
6400, which is the point of beginning.  (Ord. 11385 § 1, 1994).</span></p>

