text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Statutory provisions: Generally - chapters 9.41 and 9.45
RCW; Minors - chapter 26.28 RCW and RCW 77.32.155.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.78.010  Person defined - singular words
– words referring to specific gender.</b>  &quot;Person&quot; wherever used in
this chapter means and includes natural persons of any sex, firms,
copartnerships and corporations, whether acting by themselves, by servant,
agent or employee.  The singular number includes the plural and words referring
to a specific gender may be extended to any other gender.  (Ord. 18670 § 56,
2018:  Res. 1439 § 1, 1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.78.020  Supplying firearms or
ammunition to minor unlawful.</b>  It is unlawful for any person in King
County, state of Washington, outside the boundaries of incorporated cities and
towns within King County, to sell, barter, hire, loan or give, or permit to be
sold, bartered, hired, loaned or given to any minor under the age of twenty&#8209;one
years, any revolver, pistol or similar firearms or any ammunition for the
same.  (Res. 33741 (part), 1967: Res. 1439 § 2, 1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.78.030  Written consent required to
supply airgun or slingshot to minor.</b>  It is unlawful for any person outside
the boundaries of incorporated cities and towns within King County, Washington,
to sell, barter, hire, loan or give or permit to be sold, bartered, hired,
loaned or given to any minor under the age of eighteen years, or knowingly to
permit such minor to use or have in possession any spring gun, air gun, or any
ammunition for such a gun, or any sling or slingshot, without having first
obtained the written consent or permission of the parent or guardian having the
custody or control of the minor.  (Res. 14349 § 3, 1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.78.040  Written consent to be kept as
evidence.</b>  Any person required by K.C.C. 12.78.030 to secure the written
consent or permission therein required, shall keep the writing evidencing the
consent or permission in the person's possession for a period of one year.  Failure
or refusal within that time to permit any peace officer, upon demand to inspect
said writing shall be prima facie evidence of the person's violation of the
provisions of K.C.C. 12.78.030.  (Ord. 18670 § 57, 2018:  Res. 14349 § 4,
1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.78.050  Violation &#8209; misdemeanor.</b> 
Any person violating or failing to comply with any provisions of this chapter
shall be deemed guilty of a misdemeanor as defined by the laws of the state of
Washington and upon conviction thereof shall be subject to such punishment as
is provided by the laws of the state of Washington upon conviction for a
misdemeanor.  (Res. 14349 § 5, 1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;text-align:
justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc141867240">12.80   FURNISHING LIQUOR TO MINORS*</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            12.80.010      Possession of liquor unlawful for minor.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            12.80.020      Supplying liquor to minor unlawful.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            12.80.030      Penalty for violation.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.80.010  Possession of liquor unlawful
for minor.</b>  It is unlawful for any person under the age of twenty&#8209;one
years to acquire in any manner, consume, or have in the person's possession any
intoxicating liquor as defined by RCW 66.04.200; provided, that the foregoing
shall not apply in the case of liquor given or permitted to be given to a
person under the age of twenty&#8209;one years by the person's parent or
guardian for medicinal purposes, or administered to the person by the person's
physician or dentist for medicinal purposes.  (Ord. 18670 § 58, 2018:  Res.
13839 § 1, 1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.80.020  Supplying liquor to minor
unlawful.</b>  It is unlawful for any person to give, or otherwise supply,
intoxicating liquor to any person under the age of twenty&#8209;one years or
permit any person under that age to consume intoxicating liquor on the person's
premises or on any premises under the person's control, except as provided in K.C.C.
12.80.010.  (Ord. 18670 § 59, 2018:  Res. 13839 § 2, 1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.80.030  Penalty for violation.</b>  Any
person violating any of the provisions of Sections 12.80.010 and 12.80.020 of
this chapter shall be guilty of a misdemeanor as defined under the laws of the
state of Washington, and, upon conviction thereof, shall be punished by a fine
not exceeding one hundred dollars or by imprisonment in the county jail for not
more than thirty days.  (Res. 13839 § 3, 1953).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>*Statutory provisions &#8209; See chapter 66.44 RCW.  Driving
under the influence of intoxicating liquor or drugs &#8209; See K.C.C. chapter
20.18.</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;line-height:
normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<h1><a name="_Toc141867241">12.81   CONTROLLED SUBSTANCES</a></h1>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;line-height:normal'><span
style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>Sections:</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            12.81.010      Responsibility of persons in charge of sale
or display rooms                                                     containing
paraphernalia evincing intent to violate chapter 69.50                                             RCW.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            12.81.020      Minors prohibited unless with guardian in
places selling or displaying                                     for sale
certain paraphernalia.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            12.81.030      Sale and display room requirements.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>            12.81.040      Violation - penalty.</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;letter-spacing:
-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.81.010  Responsibility of persons in
charge of sale or display rooms containing paraphernalia evincing intent to
violate chapter 69.50 RCW.</b>  With respect to any owners, manager,
proprietor, or other person in charge of any room or enclosure in any place of
business selling, or displaying for the purpose of sale, any device,
contrivance, instrument or paraphernalia for the smoking, ingestion, injection,
or consumption of marijuana, hashish, PCP, or any controlled substance, as
defined in chapter 69.50 RCW (the Uniform Controlled Substances Act), other
than prescription drugs and devices to ingest or inject prescription drugs, as
well as roach clips, and cigarette papers and rollers designed or commonly used
for the smoking of the foregoing, no such person, under circumstances evincing the
person's intent that any such an item or items so sold or displayed be used or
employed by another in the commission of a criminal violation of chapter 69.50
RCW, shall allow or permit any person under the age of eighteen years to be,
remain in, enter, or visit such room or enclosure unless such minor person is
accompanied by one of the person's parents, or by the person's legal guardian. 
(Ord. 18670 § 60, 2018:  Ord. 4785 § 1(a), 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.81.020  Minors prohibited unless with
guardian in places selling or displaying for sale certain paraphernalia. </b> No
person under the age of eighteen years shall be, remain in, enter or visit any
room or enclosure in any place used for the sale, or displaying for sale, of
any device, contrivance, instrument or paraphernalia for the smoking,
ingestion, injection, or consumption of marijuana, hashish, PCP, or any
controlled substance, as defined in chapter 69.50 RCW (the Uniform Controlled
Substances Act), other than prescription drugs and devices to ingest or inject
prescription drugs, as well as roach clips, and cigarette papers and rollers
designed or commonly used for smoking the foregoing, under circumstances evincing
the intent of the person in charge of such room or  enclosure that any such
item or items so sold or displayed be used or employed by another in the
commission of a criminal violation of chapter 69.50 RCW, unless such person
under the age of eighteen years is accompanied by one of the person's parents,
or by the person's legal guardian.  (Ord. 18670 § 61, 2018:  Ord. 4785 § 1(b),
1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><b><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></b></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.81.030  Sale and display room
requirements.</b>  No person shall maintain in any place of business to which
the public is invited the display for sale, or the offering to sell, of any
device, contrivance, instrument or paraphernalia for the smoking, ingestion,
injection, or consumption of marijuana, hashish, PCP, or any controlled
substance, as defined in chapter 69.50 RCW (the Uniform Controlled Substances
Act), other than prescription drugs and devices to ingest or inject
prescription drugs, as well as roach clips, and cigarette papers and rollers
designed or commonly used for smoking the foregoing, under circumstances evincing
the person's intent that any such item or items so sold or displayed be used or
employed by another in the commission of criminal violation of chapter 69.50
RCW, unless within a separate room or enclosure to which minors not accompanied
by a parent or legal guardian are excluded.  At each entrance to such a room or
enclosure shall be a sign posted in reasonably visible and legible words to the
effect that minors unless accompanied by a parent or legal guardian are
excluded.  (Ord. 18670 § 62, 2018:  Ord. 4785 § 1(c), 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.81.040  Violation &#8209; penalty.</b> 
Any violation of this chapter is a misdemeanor, and the punishment shall be as
provided by the laws of the state of Washington.  (Ord. 4785 § 2, 1980).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:8.0pt;text-align:
justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>&nbsp;</span></p>

