text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.82.010  Maps to be filed with clerk of
council.</b>  Pursuant to RCW 69.50.435, for the purpose of providing a public
record of the location and boundaries of certain areas within which enhanced
penalties shall be imposed upon conviction of unlawful transactions in
controlled substances, any map depicting the location and boundaries of public
parks and of the area on or within one thousand feet of any property used for
schools which is produced or reproduced by the county executive or the engineer
of any municipality or school district and approved by the governing body of
such public agency may be filed with the clerk of the county council.  (Ord.
10154 § 1, 1991).</span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'> </span></p>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-bottom:0in;margin-bottom:0in;margin-top:0in;
text-align:justify;line-height:normal'><span style='font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;
letter-spacing:-.1pt'>            <b>12.82.020  Preparation of parks maps by
county.</b>  The county executive is directed to prepare and submit to the
council for approval by ordinance, maps showing the boundaries and locations,
including municipal boundaries, of all lands in unincorporated King County
which are operated as parks by the state or by local government and of all
county parks whether in incorporated or unincorporated areas of King County. 
The executive is directed to send a copy of Ordinance 10154 to each city and
town in King County and to the Washington State Parks and Recreation Commission
and to send a copy of each approved map to the commission and to each city or
town within whose boundaries a park is depicted.  (Ord. 10154 § 2, 1991).</span></p>

